6"><label/><p>NHS&#x0003d;Nurses' Health Study; HPFS&#x0003d;Health Professionals Follow-Up Study; RR&#x0003d;relative risk; CI&#x0003d;confidence interval.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote7"><label>a</label><p>Quartile cutpoints for men: &#x0003c;0.723; 0.723&#x02013;0.805; 0.806&#x02013;0.911; &#x0003e;0.911; and women: &#x0003c;0.687; 0.687&#x02013;0.763; 0.764&#x02013;0.839; &#x0003e;0.839.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote8"><label>b</label><p>Conditional regression analysis (matched factors: age, month of toenail collection, smoking status).</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote9"><label>c</label><p>Additionally controlling for pack-years smoked (continuous) and current heavy cigarette smoking at baseline (25&#x0002b; per day).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>